# Restore two-way compatibility for Oak Session assertion binding tokens.
#
# Oak f509cc9b5 switched to signing length-prefixed assertion binding tokens,
# and 06903274a removed the legacy verification fallback. Peers running Oak
# f7393a19 (the KMS release currently in prod) only verify the legacy token, so
# KMS replicas on different versions cannot complete their bidirectional
# handshakes during a rolling update (b/582926369).
#
# This is the pending Oak change Iab5a4dff9dd3244e792c127da87f3b2b5c20e724
# (patchset 1, 651cac12), restricted to oak_session. It signs self-assertions
# with the legacy token by default and verifies both the length-prefixed and the
# legacy token. oak_session is identical in fe9cc4a2 and the change's base
# (d8e04738), so it applies unchanged.
#
# Remove this patch once all KMS deployments verify both formats and the KMS
# opts into `SessionConfigBuilder::use_length_prefixed_binding_token()`.
